---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import winstonAvatar from '../assets/images/winston-avatar.jpg';
---

<Layout title="About | Winston Koh | AI Systems Architect" description="Explore the technical framework and philosophy of Winston Koh. Building high-leverage AI systems and sovereign digital assets.">
    <section class="about-header-flex">
        <Image src={winstonAvatar} alt="Winston Koh Illustration" class="brand-avatar" loading="eager" />
        <div class="header-text">
            <h1>About</h1>
            <p class="page-subtitle">Strategic Systems Architect & Full-stack Engineer</p>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
        <h2>The Architect</h2>
        <p>
            I'm an INTJ (Architect) with a Strategist-first orientation. I treat challenges as systems
            to be understood — diagnose the physics first, then design around them.
        </p>
        <p>
            My approach: identify the constraints of the arena, design a system that navigates them,
            and execute with precision.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
        <h2>Background</h2>
        <div class="timeline">
            <div class="timeline-item">
                <span class="timeline-label">Education</span>
                <p>15 years experience. BBM (Finance & Corp Comms), SMU 2011.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="timeline-item">
                <span class="timeline-label">Credentials</span>
                <p>CFA Level 1, ChFC®/S, CLU®/S, CFP® Modules 1-6, ACTA</p>
            </div>
            <div class="timeline-item">
                <span class="timeline-label">Evolution</span>
                <p>Finance → Insurance → Curriculum Development → Systems Architecture</p>
            </div>
            <div class="timeline-item">
                <span class="timeline-label">2026</span>
                <p><a href="/services/" style="color: inherit; text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.3);">Ghost Brand Ecosystems</a>, Zero-Point Architecture, Anti-Slop Protocol</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
        <h2>Philosophy: The Anti-Slop Protocol</h2>
        <p>
            I navigate reality as it <strong>IS</strong>, not as it <strong>SHOULD BE</strong>. In an era of AI-generated noise ("Slop"), 
            <a href="/articles/anti-slop-protocol/" style="color: inherit; text-decoration: underline;">signaling requires <strong>friction</strong></a>.
        </p>
        <p>
            This isn't cynicism — it's operational clarity. Moralism is a luxury; physics is mandatory.
            The question isn't "Is this fair?" but "What are the actual forces at play, and how do I
            position myself to survive them?"
        </p>
        <blockquote>
            "Navigate, don't litigate."
        </blockquote>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
        <h2>The Bionic Operating Model</h2>
        <p>
            I operate as a <a href="/articles/ai-bionic-layer/" style="color: inherit; text-decoration: underline;"><strong>bionic unit</strong></a> — human cognition augmented by AI at every layer.
        </p>
        <div class="highlight-box">
            <p><strong>Human Intent</strong> (Top 1% Nuance) + <strong>AI Scale</strong> (Bottom 99% Execution) =
                <strong>1000% Leverage</strong>
            </p>
        </div>
        <p>
            This follows the <strong>Architectural Isomorphism</strong> principle: The User provides the Meta-Cognition (How to think), 
            and the AI provides the Execution (What to do).
        </p>
        <p>
            The AI isn't a replacement; it's a force multiplier. I provide strategic direction and
            high-nuance judgment. The AI handles research, execution, and documentation at scale.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
        <h2>AI Proficiency</h2>
        <p>
            I work with <strong>state-of-the-art frontier models</strong> daily — not as a casual user, but as a practitioner who understands prompt engineering, agentic workflows, and how to orchestrate AI systems for production-grade output.
        </p>
        <div class="stack-grid">
            <div class="stack-category">
                <h3>Frontier Models (2026)</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Google:</strong> Gemini 3.1 Pro, Gemini 3 Flash</li>
                    <li><strong>xAI:</strong> Grok 4.1 (Thinking)</li>
                    <li><strong>Anthropic:</strong> Claude Opus 4.6 (Thinking)</li>
                    <li><strong>OpenAI:</strong> GPT-5.2, GPT-5.1-High</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="stack-category">
                <h3>AI Capabilities</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Prompt Engineering:</strong> System prompts, few-shot, chain-of-thought</li>
                    <li><strong>Agentic Development:</strong> Multi-step autonomous workflows</li>
                    <li><strong>RAG Systems:</strong> Vector search, semantic retrieval, knowledge graphs</li>
                    <li><strong>AI Image/Video:</strong> Midjourney, DALL-E, Runway, Veo 2</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
        <p style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">
            Every project I ship is <strong>AI-native</strong> — from research and design to code and content. This isn't "using ChatGPT"; it's running a bionic production pipeline.
        </p>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
        <h2>The Stack</h2>
        <div class="stack-grid">
            <div class="stack-category">
                <h3>Preferred Tools</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Agentic IDE:</strong> Google Antigravity</li>
                    <li><strong>Reasoning:</strong> Claude Opus 4.6, Gemini 3.1 Pro, Gemini 3 Flash</li>
                    <li><strong>Frontend:</strong> Astro (Static Site Generator)</li>
                    <li><strong>Backend:</strong> Python, Supabase (pgvector)</li>
                    <li><strong>Architecture:</strong> Flat-file Markdown, Protocol-Driven</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
            <div class="stack-category">
                <h3>Hard Passes</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Black-box RAG:</strong> If I can't audit the retrieval, I don't use it.</li>
                    <li><strong>Bloated Frameworks:</strong> No LangChain/AutoGPT. Primitives only.</li>
                    <li><strong>Platform-Locked Memory:</strong> My context stays in Markdown.</li>
                </ul>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section">
        <h2>Current Project: <a href="/athena/" style="color: inherit; text-decoration: none;">Athena</a> (v9.9.1)</h2>
        <p>
            <a href="/athena/" style="color: inherit; text-decoration: underline;">Athena</a> is an AI-Powered Digital Personal Assistant operating on the <strong>Zero-Point Codex</strong> architecture.
            It enforces the <strong>Triple-Lock Protocol</strong> (Search → Save → Speak) to ensure every output is grounded in context.
        </p>
        <p>
            It's not a chatbot. It's a living architecture of protocols, frameworks, case studies,
            and calibrated insights that compounds over time. Every conversation becomes intellectual
            capital.
        </p>
        <a href="https://github.com/winstonkoh87/Athena-Public" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"
            class="text-link">
            View the public repository →
        </a>
    </section>

    <section class="content-section" style="text-align: center; padding-top: 2rem;">
        <h2>Want to work together?</h2>
        <p style="color: #8892b0;">Internal AI systems. Ops automation. Knowledge engines.</p>
        <a href="/contact/" class="btn btn-primary" style="margin-top: 1rem;">Get in touch →</a>
    </section>
</Layout>
